mode: "100644"
text: "# Element Playbook\n\nEvery profile element has a **job**. \"Fill it in\" isn't optimization — making each element do its job\nis. Here's each one, what it's for, and how to optimize it.\n\n## Handle / username\n\n- **Job:** be searchable, memorable, consistent. Ideally your name or brand; easy to spell and say.\n- **Do:** keep it the **same across platforms** (recognition + cross-platform discovery). Avoid\n  number/underscore soup. A niche keyword in the handle helps local/service accounts (e.g.,\n  `@austinhomeexpert`).\n\n## Name / display field (the most-wasted field)\n\n- **Job:** this field is **searchable and indexed** (Instagram weighs it heavily in search; LinkedIn\n  the headline). It's how people find you by *what you do*, not just your name.\n- **Do:** put **name + a niche keyword** — \"Jane Doe | SaaS Growth\", \"Austin Realtor | Jane Smith\".\n  Don't waste it on just \"Jane ✨\". Think like your audience: what would they *search*?\n- Note the character limit is tight (see `platform-specs.md`) — lead with the keyword that matters.\n\n## Profile picture\n\n- **Job:** instant recognition at thumbnail size.\n- **Do:** **a clear face for personal brands/creators** (faces build trust and convert), a clean\n  **logo/mark for companies**. High contrast, recognizable small, **consistent across platforms**.\n  No busy, low-res, or zoomed-out shots.\n\n## Bio — the pitch\n\n- **Job:** pass the 3-second test and earn the follow. Who you help · what you do · why follow · CTA.\n- **The formula (adapt, keep it human):**\n  1. **Who + what** — \"I help [audience] [outcome]\" or \"[What you make] for [who].\"\n  2. **Proof / credibility** — a specific number, credential, or notable (\"+300 projects,\" \"ex-X,\"\n     \"trusted by N teams\"). Real only.\n  3. **CTA + link prompt** — the next step (\"Free playbook ↓\", \"DM 'GROW'\", \"Book a call ↓\").\n- **Do:** clarity first, personality second; **skimmable lines**; tight (respect the limit); keywords\n  for search; emojis as sparing signposts, not clutter. Cut filler (\"Welcome to my page!\" wastes\n  space). On-voice (`voice.md`).\n\n## Link / link-in-bio — the conversion mechanism\n\n- **Job:** turn the visit into an action.\n- **Do:** **match the link to the current goal/CTA** (one clear destination beats a junk drawer). If\n  you need several, use a tidy **link hub** that **leads with the priority action**, not 15 equal\n  links. Update it per campaign. Make the bio say *why* to click (the result they get), not just\n  \"link in bio.\" Use a trackable link where possible (native insights, not WoopSocial analytics).\n\n## CTA\n\n- **Job:** tell the visitor the one next step. Don't make them guess.\n- **Do:** pick **one** primary action aligned to the goal (follow / subscribe / shop / book /\n  download / DM). Make it explicit in the bio and on the pinned content.\n\n## Pinned / featured posts\n\n- **Job:** control the first impression beyond the bio — your \"best of.\"\n- **Do:** pin posts that **introduce you**, **prove value**, or **convert** (a strong intro, a\n  best-performer, a clear offer). On LinkedIn use **Featured**; on X/TikTok/IG, pin to the top.\n\n## Highlights (Instagram) / categorized evergreen\n\n- **Job:** answer \"tell me more\" without scrolling.\n- **Do:** a few clear categories — **Start here / About**, **Proof / results**, **What I offer /\n  Products**, **FAQ**. Clean, on-brand covers; ordered by priority.\n\n## Banner / header (LinkedIn, X, YouTube, Facebook)\n\n- **Job:** prime real estate at the top of the profile — most people waste it on a stock photo.\n- **Do:** make it carry a **value prop, proof, or CTA** plus visual brand. Provide a **banner brief**\n  (what it should say/show), and hand the visual to a designer or an image tool\n  (`tools/integrations/ideogram.md` / `nano-banana.md`) — Ideogram is good for legible text on a\n  banner.\n\n## Category / contact & action buttons (business profiles)\n\n- **Job:** enable the action.\n- **Do:** set the right **category**, enable **contact/book/shop** buttons where the goal needs them.\n\n## The deliverable\n\nFor each element, hand the user **ready-to-paste copy or a clear spec** — not advice to \"improve your\nbio,\" but the actual bio, name field, CTA, link choice, pinned plan, highlights plan, and banner\nbrief, each passing the 3-second test.\n"
